<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Brazil's Lula reelected president in runoff vote: A look back at his career</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8f4e4d6bc2a4eab5f0bad1a1e30ced4c18b4919c399ad60201377dfdff21ec7</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T15:11:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-reelected-president-in-runoff-vote-a-look-back-at-his-career" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won an unprecedented fourth term on Sunday (October 25), the country's electoral court said, in a shock result that defied polls.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms 2026: A history of gerrymandering</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cb4094f2907c8b0774ee3ed803aeb56c9722b577995978f730a718dbc08a3b3</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:48:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-2026-a-history-of-gerrymandering" /><summary type="html">What does a salamander have to do with US elections? Dating back centuries, gerrymandering continues to play a role in American elections today. Used more often by Republicans in the modern era of voting, Democrats have also resorted to the tactic in the past decade. But what is gerrymandering, and why is it called that? FRANCE 24's Tanishk Saha explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Obama blasts Trump's 'chaos and cruelty' while campaigning for Democrats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:056e6a65a4abbee9b599c5996b1a7be4ea191ce3f346164cef81ac299705726a</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:28:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-obama-blasts-trump-s-chaos-and-cruelty-while-campaigning-for-democrats" /><summary type="html">Ten days out from the elections that will determine control of the closely divided Congress, Barack Obama took to the campaign trail to accuse the Republican president of corruption, deride his strategy for Iran and skewer the gilded aesthetic he has applied ‌to White House renovations. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula wins fourth term: What are the reactions in Brazil?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95dc46b3de28e9bc35308c932a78367c3d66a947d3fe6a355bde7396ad9a3156</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:04:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-wins-fourth-term-what-are-the-reactions-in-brazil" /><summary type="html">Brazil's leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva was re-elected against all expectations on Sunday (October 25), but his conservative rival Flavio Bolsonaro refused to accept the loss and said he would seek to have the vote annulled. FRANCE 24's Jan Onoszko tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bolsonaro's refusal to concede underscores ‘serious’ challenges to Brazil's democratic institutions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcf87f1b691b11337107e2d6ac3790df2a7a49c2c9e2e83ae38c51088c4d63e0</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:53:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-refusal-to-concede-underscores-serious-challenges-to-brazil-s-democratic-institutions" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome Dr Pedro Perfeito da Silva, Latin American specialist at the University of Exeter. For Dr Perfeito da Silva, Lula's stunning success reflects the convergence of digital organizing, grassroots mobilization, targeted socioeconomic appeals and an effective effort to mobilise opposition to the Bolsonaro political project. As he explains, Lula assembled a coalition that "not only energized his supporters but also attracted voters from groups that had been somewhat skeptical of the government in the first round."</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula wins Brazil election but faces uphill battle to govern</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25eb04da2b3bb28cce718d9c54ea158bd70de016e76928df284248eb644eb109</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:38:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-lula-wins-brazil-election-but-faces-uphill-battle-to-govern" /><summary type="html">Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's narrow election victory on Sunday has dealt a blow to Brazil's far right, but deep political divisions remain. The newly re-elected president must tackle economic and security concerns at home while navigating international tensions with US President Donald Trump.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Lula beats Bolsonaro in Brazil runoff: What does it mean for Donald Trump?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03a7c67607da310c9ff13e9daa116fe8707393255d2d6d380c3c044cd7944b76</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:50:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-lula-beats-bolsonaro-in-brazil-runoff-what-does-it-mean-for-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">Lula defeated on Sunday (October 25) Flavio Bolsonaro in Brazil’s presidential election. But rather than conceding, Bolsonaro called for the result to be annulled. As the US midterms approach, the result raises questions about Trump’s influence and how his political allies respond when voters reject them. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor, Douglas Herbert, gives us his analysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Trump's gains among Latino voters in Texas at risk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c26f1902719d18929b56f4955111b875b51fcac7eb3abb7e93e38da65145f2f</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:42:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-us-midterms-trump-s-gains-among-latino-voters-in-texas-at-risk" /><summary type="html">Latino voters shifted toward Trump two years ago, helping him return to the White House with a Republican-controlled Congress. Now, many are souring on the US president and his party. FRANCE 24's team reports from the Rio Grande Valley.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil: What challenges await Lula in his fourth term as president?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3331721641c947f4e788b8b3dff9e7bff6bd35c6919d99eed2ef86502c145565</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:46:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-what-challenges-await-lula-in-his-fourth-term-as-president" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, nearly 81 years old, clinched a fourth term in a tight runoff against Flavio Bolsonaro on Sunday (October 25). He will have to wrestle with a divided Brazil, an unfriendly Congress, feeble public finances and a Donald Trump-shaped menace during his unprecedented fourth term.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula wins historic fourth term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eea74cb189f36de4fb441c498a1f64f2a73df6cb9ee5ae45a0eaa0f44635fc3b</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:44:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-wins-historic-fourth-term" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, nearly 81 years old, clinched a fourth term in a tight runoff against Flavio Bolsonaro on Sunday (October 26). The leftist leader won 51.7% of the vote, compared to 48.2% for the son of former president Jair Bolsonaro, official results showed. Bolsonaro has refused to accept the loss and said he would seek to annul the vote.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula seals re-election in surprise win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f98b225441fdb65919bd08adfd90626b453598e2d0c66e9e03686728536852b7</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:33:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-seals-re-election-in-surprise-win" /><summary type="html">Brazil's President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won an unprecedented fourth term in a tight runoff against Flavio Bolsonaro on Sunday (October 25). The far-right candidate and son of former President Jair Bolsonaro has refused to accept the results and said he would seek to annul the vote.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Congratulations!’: World leaders hail Lula’s election victory in Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c6a6f03a45e099fec1d8c2ccbafd5d49ce6a6176170bc7145cba5fd03b6a170</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:31:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-congratulations-world-leaders-hail-lula-s-election-victory-in-brazil" /><summary type="html">The international community on Monday congratulated Brazil's President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva after his stunning re-election in a runoff with right-wing candidate Flavio Bolsonaro. The region's left-leaning leaders were quick to react as Brazil staved off a conservative wave in many countries while Europeans, such as Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez, celebrated a "progressive comeback".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Lula's 'extraordinary victory' faces growing middle class, deeply-entrenched bolsonarismo &amp; Big Tech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f43649588abae816510caa730706ce2f4795fa1666777029fe7b6a6aa1728634</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T08:41:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-s-extraordinary-victory-faces-growing-middle-class-deeply-entrenched-bolsonarismo-big-tech" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Dr Felipe Krause, Political Scientist, former Diplomat and Departmental Lecturer in Latin American Studies at the Oxford School of Global and Area Studies.  Beneath Lula's electoral triumph lies a more complex political reality: the Brazilian hard right has consolidated its influence across state governments and legislative institutions, raising fundamental questions about the balance of power and the future of progressive governance. Lula will be focusing more on "working to keep things from eroding" rather than advancing his progressive agenda, explains Dr. Krause. 'There is more need for economic measures that support the growing middle class."</summary></entry><entry><title>What challenges await Brazil's Lula in his fourth term as president?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1f3f0af4bfb156d4d0d35524c5cc5cfbbd09a166f77749006ee141f3bc104de</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T00:52:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-what-challenges-await-brazil-s-lula-in-his-fourth-term-as-president" /><summary type="html">President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva will have to wrestle with a divided Brazil, an unfriendly Congress, feeble public finances and a Donald Trump-shaped menace during his unprecedented fourth term.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula beats odds and seals re-election, rival Bolsonaro demands annulment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5626ff7fca679d48635bf09cfa8427ee5c7c900a8b862c6a32fba7ec3fd4795a</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T00:23:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-brazil-s-president-lula-da-silva-beats-flavio-bolsonaro-to-win-re-election" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, nearly 81 years old, clinched a fourth term in a tight runoff against Flavio Bolsonaro on Sunday. The leftist leader won 51.7% of the vote, compared to 48.2% for the son of former president Jair Bolsonaro, official results showed. Bolsonaro has refused to accept the loss and said he would seek to annul the vote.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil presidential election: Lula's late surge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaa23862134a120c0e7e2186a4419cae66b9e8ea9bee86b916491101388d7471</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T19:00:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261025-lula-s-legacy-flavio-s-future--edbc5d7dfc1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261025-lula-s-legacy-flavio-s-future" /><summary type="html">It's a coin-flip election in Brazil, with little separating the country's left-wing President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his far-right rival Flavio Bolsonaro. The results of the run-off vote will become clear in a few hours.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Opposition leader Machado returns to Venezuela after 10 months in exile</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df811598f82ffc3367b34708d99f7ca5d4bf674d03c75283e3752ae639e362f7</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T17:10:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-opposition-leader-machado-returns-to-venezuela-after-10-months-in-exile--1872e0f5ffc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-opposition-leader-machado-returns-to-venezuela-after-10-months-in-exile" /><summary type="html">Venezuelan opposition leader Maria Corina Machado announced on Sunday that she has returned to her homeland following almost a year in exile, after covertly leaving Venezuela in late 2025 to receive the Nobel Peace Prize. She returns as doubts about her country’s democratic future and the role of the US are growing.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Presidential runoff under way in Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f1eed0b6a28ecdab704e965dab35d0de6a58996a7e4854715c89d571d8f8129</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T13:52:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/presidential-runoff-under-way-in-brazil--bf9c7e32c5bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/presidential-runoff-under-way-in-brazil" /><summary type="html">Brazil is also heading to the polls today for a run-off vote that will decide who leads the country. The race is on a knife edge between incumbent left-wing President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and right-wing Senator Flávio Bolsonaro. The son of former president Jair Bolsonaro, Flávio scored a major upset in the first round earlier this month, taking the lead in the vote. The campaign has been dominated by corruption scandals, economic difficulties and allegations of US interference, which Washington has denied. France 24 correspondent Jan Onoszko reports the latest from Rio de Janeiro.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula thanks voters for his victory, Bolsonaro does not recognise the results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9192a2df1a7d19968568812c31bba71c4e6599e0e862585401cd009fdf667bc8</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T12:46:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-live-voting-under-way-across-brazil-in-tight-presidential-run-off-between-lula-and-bolsonar--05fa1f528dbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-live-voting-under-way-across-brazil-in-tight-presidential-run-off-between-lula-and-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">It is the first time in Brazil's history since the return of democracy in the country that a candidate who lost in the first round managed to come back and win in the runoff. The left-wing president Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva obtained 51.7% of the votes, compared with 48.2% won by right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Polls open in Brazil presidential runoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58d2ea463d55063ef081a43445bcea160ed06906c77b83a43b744fdd63071444</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:40:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/polls-open-in-brazil-presidential-runoff--8d55229e95d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/polls-open-in-brazil-presidential-runoff" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and sight-wing senator Flavio Bolsonaro faced off Friday in their second and final debate ahead of Sunday's presidential runoff election. The two candidates repeated their campaign proposals, focusing on the cost of living and security, while exchanging ⁠allegations of corruption. France 24 Jan Onoszko telles us the latest from Rio de Janeiro.</summary></entry><entry><title>Obama hits campaign trail for democrats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9f299f3646c8915623239cc31ea821852998cf4b50bda5c829900720bb24524</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:36:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/obama-hits-campaign-trail-for-democrats--dc300583e461.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/obama-hits-campaign-trail-for-democrats" /><summary type="html">With less than two weeks to go before the US midterm elections, former President Barack Obama has hit the campaign trail, rallying support for Democratic candidates in the key states of Michigan and Ohio. He criticised the Trump administration, blaming the White House for rising living costs, a major concern for voters. Democrats are hoping to regain control of Congress, with polls showing several closely contested races. Ophelie Jacobson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>What to know as Brazilians choose between Lula and Flavio Bolsonaro in tense presidential run-off</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d9b2ba442c14d7c494ccebeff5d2709e2ba8151c31ea75c210d3c87fc328e18</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T06:05:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-what-to-know-as-brazilians-choose-between-lula-and-bolsonaro-in-tense-presidential-runoff--2a6bd58b70ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-what-to-know-as-brazilians-choose-between-lula-and-bolsonaro-in-tense-presidential-runoff" /><summary type="html">Brazilians are set on Sunday to choose between leftist incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and far-right candidate Flavio Bolsonaro in the run-off vote of a deeply polarizing presidential election, and one which will determine whether the US significantly expands its growing influence in Latin America.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US seeks to topple Cuba's government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7cdc927c1dd8b85f7f1afc172d2547bebca093231ff5c8e02437c18e83d7918</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:43:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-seeks-to-topple-cuba-s-government--b52eb58eab6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-seeks-to-topple-cuba-s-government" /><summary type="html">And now, in a rather surprising development, US Secretary of State Marco Rubio is directly urging Cubans to cooperate with the CIA. Havana has responded by mocking what it calls the Trump administration’s “desperation”.</summary></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump challenges Alaska Senate trace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7648ad5ee5e79c8c6a0283dddb0c35f55b13d306dc0db6a9da2bcc6867226421</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:42:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-challenges-alaska-senate-trace--8639a06bdbc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-challenges-alaska-senate-trace" /><summary type="html">With the US midterm elections less than two weeks away, concerns are growing over whether President Donald Trump would accept a major Republican defeat. Trump has called for legal action to block the certification of Alaska’s Senate race if Republican incumbent Dan Sullivan loses to his Democratic challenger, Mary Peltola, arguing that another candidate with the same name on the ballot could confuse voters. Our Washington correspondent Fraser Jackson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump administration sues to block possible Democratic win in Alaska Senate race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8d14d0bd68c5cefa3d123c95ad0ce904e7e70a929d7f1a0ab3b7216c272424a</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:40:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261024-trump-administration-sues-to-block-possible-democratic-win-in-alaska-senate-race--2cdc4eae1c83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261024-trump-administration-sues-to-block-possible-democratic-win-in-alaska-senate-race" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Friday that he had instructed his administration to file a lawsuit to block the certification of the US Senate race in Alaska if Republican Senator Dan Sullivan loses, arguing that voters would be confused because two Republicans on the ballot have similar names. The legal battle is ramping up questions over whether Trump will accept a potential midterms defeat.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says US may launch ‘another little Epic Fury’ attack on Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b344a0ba9efebf4520c8562f4c62ae2b598d91ca98482ee83b6b04cdbc63678</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T20:50:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-trump-says-us-may-launch-another-little-epic-fury-attack-iran--267a801616fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-trump-says-us-may-launch-another-little-epic-fury-attack-iran" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Friday said his country may launch “another little Epic Fury” on Iran, referring to the joint Israeli-American military operation that sparked the war with Iran at the end of February.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's tense presidential run-off campaign feels like a psychological thriller</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:faa64628fc0054db6ee7d770346625b25a71fb2e6321a4ea6457b82d6eed0f1b</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:45:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-brazil-s-tense-presidential-run-off-campaign-feels-like-a-psychological-thriller--934b659fa2c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-brazil-s-tense-presidential-run-off-campaign-feels-like-a-psychological-thriller" /><summary type="html">Insults traded on social media and a combative debate have intensified the pressure ahead of a fiercely contested presidential run-off on Sunday, with only a few points separating leftist pro-union President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and far-right challenger Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of former president and Trump ally Jair Bolsonaro.</summary>